.TH SCOOP-AI 1 "2026-06-18" "0.1.0" "Scoop Manifest Generator"
.SH NAME
scoop-ai \- AI agent that generates Scoop manifests for Windows packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scoop-ai
[\fI\,SUBCOMMAND\/\fR] [\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR]
.P
.B scoop-ai
\fI\,URL\/\fR [\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR]
.P
.B scoop-ai generate
\fI\,URL\/\fR [\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR]
.P
.B scoop-ai doctor
.P
.B scoop-ai config show
.P
.B scoop-ai completion
\fI\,SHELL\/\fR
.P
.B scoop-ai version
.SH DESCRIPTION
scoop-ai is an AI-powered manifest generator for the Scoop package manager
on Windows. Given a GitHub repository URL, it automatically researches the
project, analyzes Windows release assets, and generates a standards-compliant
Scoop bucket manifest.
.P
The generation uses a three-phase LLM agent workflow:
.IP \(bu 3
.B Research
\- Gather project metadata, discover Windows release assets via GitHub API,
and identify persist targets from source code.
.IP \(bu 3
.B Analyze
\- Compute SHA-256 hashes, inspect archive contents (ZIP, MSI, portable),
and determine the correct bin, shortcuts, and extract_dir.
.IP \(bu 3
.B Generate
\- Create the Scoop manifest JSON, validate it against Scoop's schema,
and write it to the output file.
.P
If the first argument is not a subcommand name and does not start with \-,
it is treated as a URL and the
.B generate
subcommand is automatically prepended.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B generate \fI\,URL\/\fR [\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR]
Generate a Scoop manifest from a GitHub repository URL or project URL.
This is the primary command. If no subcommand is given and a URL is
provided, generate is implied.
.TP
.B doctor
Run 7 environment health checks:
jdk-version, os, scoop-installed, api-key, cache-dir, write-permission,
and version. Exits with code 0 on success (warnings allowed), code 1 on
failure.
.TP
.B config show
Display the runtime configuration after merging environment variables and
defaults. API keys are shown as "set" or "unset" only.
.TP
.B completion \fI\,SHELL\/\fR
Generate shell completion scripts. Supported shells: bash, zsh, fish,
powershell.
.TP
.B version
Print the scoop-ai version and commit hash.
.SH OPTIONS
The following options apply to the
.B generate
subcommand and the implicit URL mode.
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output=\fI\,PATH\/\fR
Output file path. Default: bucket/<app>.json.
.TP
.B \-P, \-\-provider=\fI\,PROVIDER\/\fR
LLM provider. One of: deepseek, openai, anthropic, ollama, openrouter,
openai-compatible. Default: deepseek.
.TP
.B \-\-api\-key=\fI\,KEY\/\fR
LLM API key. Overrides the provider-specific environment variable.
.TP
.B \-\-base\-url=\fI\,URL\/\fR
Custom API base URL. Required for the openai-compatible provider.
.TP
.B \-m, \-\-model=\fI\,MODEL\/\fR
LLM model name. Overrides the provider default.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-verify
Run 'scoop install' to verify the generated manifest.
.TP
.B \-\-app\-name=\fI\,NAME\/\fR
Application name for output path and cache. Inferred from URL by default.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Do not keep downloaded files in the Scoop cache after generation.
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-prompt=\fI\,TEXT\/\fR
Additional instructions for the manifest generation agent.
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-non\-interactive
Skip interactive prompts. Suitable for batch or CI mode.
.TP
.B \-\-github\-token=\fI\,TOKEN\/\fR
GitHub personal access token. Avoids rate limits during the research phase.
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-persist=\fI\,MODE\/\fR
Persist field policy. One of: auto, force, none, no. Default: auto.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Print debug information including stack traces.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-progress
Disable the TTY progress overlay.
.TP
.B \-\-output\-format=\fI\,FORMAT\/\fR
Output format. One of: text, json. Default: text.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SCOOP_AI_API_KEY
Fallback API key for all providers. Overridden by provider-specific keys.
.TP
.B SCOOP_AI_PROVIDER
LLM provider name. Default: deepseek.
.TP
.B SCOOP_AI_BASE_URL
Custom API base URL.
.TP
.B SCOOP_AI_MODEL
LLM model name override.
.TP
.B SCOOP_AI_OUTPUT
Default output file path.
.TP
.B SCOOP_AI_VERIFY
Set to "true" to enable install verification by default.
.TP
.B SCOOP_AI_DEBUG
Set to "true" to enable debug output.
.TP
.B SCOOP_AI_GITHUB_TOKEN
GitHub personal access token (fallback).
.TP
.B DEEPSEEK_API_KEY
DeepSeek provider API key.
.TP
.B OPENAI_API_KEY
OpenAI provider API key.
.TP
.B ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
Anthropic provider API key.
.TP
.B OPENROUTER_API_KEY
OpenRouter provider API key.
.TP
.B GITHUB_TOKEN
GitHub personal access token.
.TP
.B GH_TOKEN
GitHub token alias.
.TP
.B HTTP_PROXY, HTTPS_PROXY
Proxy server URL for HTTP and HTTPS traffic.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Set to "1" to disable ANSI color output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Operation completed successfully.
.TP
1
General error (unexpected failure).
.TP
2
Invalid command-line arguments or usage (USAGE).
.TP
3
Configuration error, e.g. missing \-\-base\-url for openai-compatible (CONFIG).
.TP
64
No Windows assets found for the given project (NO_ASSETS).
.TP
65
LLM provider error, e.g. API failure or timeout (LLM_ERROR).
.TP
66
Manifest verification (scoop install) failed (VERIFY_FAILED).
.TP
70
File I/O error, e.g. write failure or network error (IO_ERROR).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Generate a manifest with default settings
.B scoop-ai https://github.com/sharkdp/fd
.TP
Generate with a specific provider and model
.B scoop-ai generate \-P openai \-m gpt-4o https://github.com/sharkdp/fd
.TP
Generate and verify with Scoop
.B scoop-ai \-\-verify https://github.com/sharkdp/fd
.TP
Force persist field discovery
.B scoop-ai \-s force https://github.com/sharkdp/fd
.TP
Run environment diagnostics
.B scoop-ai doctor
